omoDays) {\n                    apr = apr.add(acc.promoApr);\n                }\n            }\n\n            // Calculate daily interest\n            BigDecimal principal = eodBalance.compareTo(BigDecimal.ZERO) > 0 ? eodBalance : BigDecimal.ZERO;\n            BigDecimal dailyInterestRaw = principal.multiply(apr).divide(BD_365, 10, RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN);\n\n            totalInterestRaw = totalInterestRaw.add(dailyInterestRaw);\n\n            InterestRecord ir = new InterestRecord();\n            ir.accountId = accId;\n            ir.bizDate = bizDate;\n            ir.eodBalance = eodBalance;\n            ir.apr = apr;\n            ir.dailyInterest = dailyInterestRaw.setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN);\n            interestRecords.add(ir);\n        }\n\n        // Write interest.csv\n        StringBuilder interestCsv = new StringBuilder();\n        interestCsv.append(\"account_id,biz_date,eod_balance,apr,daily_interest\\n\");\n        for (InterestRecord ir : interestRecords) {\n            interestCsv.append(ir.accountId).append(\",\");\n            interestCsv.append(ir.bizDate).append(\",\");\n            interestCsv.append(formatDecimal(ir.eodBalance, 2)).append(\",\");\n            interestCsv.append(formatDecimal(ir.apr, 6)).append(\",\");\n            interestCsv.append(formatDecimal(ir.dailyInterest, 2)).append(\"\\n\");\n        }\n        writeFile(\"/app/output/interest.csv\", interestCsv.toString());","numLines":50,"startLine":155,"totalLines":633}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01T6FZsPt6wQNKg7tg7PYacd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I see that when no fee applies, the amount is not rounded to 2dp before adding to eodBalance. Let me trace through more carefully.\n\nActually, looking at the transaction file again and thinking about what valid transactions exist:\n\nA1001 (USD, PLAN_A applies to DEBIT):\n- T001: -2000 USD. Valid. DEBIT, fee applies: 0.50 + 0.005*2000 = 10.50, clamped to 5.00. adjusted = -2000 - 5 = -2005.00\n- T013: +30 GBP -> USD on 2024-02-10. CREDIT, no fee. \n\nFor GBP->USD: check direct first, then reverse.\n- Direct GBP->USD: no entries\n- Reverse USD->GBP: 2024-02-01 = 0.7900. Rate = 1/0.7900 = 1.2658227848 (10dp HALF_EVEN)\n\n30 * 1.2658227848 = 37.9746835440. No fee. adjusted = 37.9746835440\n\nBut wait, should this be rounded to 2dp? The spec says \"adjusted = amount - fee\" and that's what gets rounded. If no fee, is there an \"adjusted\" value?\n\nI think logically, every valid transaction contributes an \"adjusted\" amount to the balance. If a fee applies, adjusted = amount - fee (rounded to 2dp). If no fee applies, adjusted = amount (but should it be rounded to 2dp too?).\n\nLooking at the spec: \"adjusted = amount - fee, rounded Half-even 2dp\" - this formula is specifically about when a fee is applied. It doesn't say what happens when no fee applies.\n\nThen: \"eod_balance = start_balance + sum(valid adjusted), rounded to two decimal places\" - this sums the adjusted values and rounds.\n\nI'll assume that when no fee applies, the amount (after FX conversion) is used as-is without rounding to 2dp, and only the final eod_balance is rounded. Let me continue tracing.\n\n- T014: -10000 JPY -> USD on 2024-03-01. DEBIT, fee applies.\n\nFor JPY->USD on 2024-03-01:\n- Direct JPY->USD: none\n- Reverse USD->JPY: 2024-03-01 rate 150.00. Rate = 1/150 = 0.0066666667 (10dp HALF_EVEN)\n\nWait, 1/150 = 0.00666666666... Rounded to 10dp HALF_EVEN: 0.0066666667\n\n-10000 * 0.0066666667 = -66.66666670\n\nFee (PLAN_A, DEBIT): 0.50 + 0.005 * 66.66666670 = 0.50 + 0.33333333 = 0.83333333\nRounded to 2dp: 0.83\nClamp to [0.25, 5.00]: 0.83\n\nadjusted = -66.66666670 - 0.83 = -67.49666670\nRounded to 2dp: -67.50\n\nSo A1001:\nstart_balance = 10000.00\n+ T001 adjusted = -2005.00\n+ T013 adjusted = 37.9746835440 (no fee, not rounded)\n+ T014 adjusted = -67.50\n\neod_balance = 10000.00 - 2005.00 + 37.9746835440 - 67.50 = 7965.4746835440\nRounded to 2dp: 7965.47\n\nMy current output shows A1001 = 7965.47. Let me verify this is correct...\n\nActually wait, I need to check the fee calculation for T001 again. The amount is -2000.00.\n\nfee = flat_fee + pct_fee * abs(amount) = 0.50 + 0.005 * 2000 = 0.50 + 10.00 = 10.50\nRound to 2dp: 10.50\nClamp to [min_fee=0.25, max_fee=5.00]: 5.00\n\nadjusted = amount - fee = -2000.00 - 5.00 = -2005.00\n\nWait, this doesn't seem right. If amount is -2000 (a debit), and we subtract a fee of 5.00, we get -2005.00. That makes the balance go down more, which makes sense - the fee is deducted.\n\nFor T013 (CREDIT, no fee):\n- GBP->USD rate: 1/0.79 = 1.2658227848 (need to verify)\n\nLet me recalculate: 1 / 0.79 = 1.26582278481...\n\nBigDecimal.ONE.divide(0.79, 10, HALF_EVEN):\n1/0.79 = 1.265822784810126582...\nRounded to 10 decimal places with HALF_EVEN: 1.2658227848\n\n30 * 1.2658227848 = 37.974683544\n\nFor T014 (DEBIT, fee applies):\n- JPY->USD rate: 1/150 = 0.0066666667 (rounded 10dp HALF_EVEN)\n\nLet me recalculate: 1/150 = 0.00666666666...\nRounded to 10dp HALF_EVEN: 0.0066666667\n\n-10000 * 0.0066666667 = -66.66666670\n\nfee = 0.50 + 0.005 * 66.66666670 = 0.50 + 0.3333333335 = 0.8333333335\nRounded to 2dp: 0.83\nClamp: 0.83 (within [0.25, 5.00])\n\nadjusted = -66.66666670 - 0.83 = -67.49666670\nRounded to 2dp: -67.50\n\nTotal for A1001:\n10000.00 + (-2005.00) + 37.974683544 + (-67.50) = 7965.474683544\nRounded to 2dp: 7965.47\n\nGreat, matches my output!\n\nNow let me check A1002 (USD, PLAN_B applies to ALL):\n\nA1002 valid transactions:\n- T004 (row 4): +50 USD. CREDIT, fee applies (ALL).\n- T011 (row 12): +5 USD. CREDIT, fee applies.\n\nWait, let me trace which are valid:\n- T004 row 4: valid (first occurrence)\n- T004 row 5: DUPLICATE\n- T005 row 6: REVERSED (T006 reverses it)\n- T006 row 7: REVERSED (it's the reverser)\n- T011 row 12: valid\n- T012 row 13: AFTER_BIZ_DATE\n- T015 row 16: valid? Let me check.\n\nT015: A1002, 2024-03-01, 100.00 CAD, POSTED.\n- Not reversed\n- Not reversal_missing\n- FX_MISSING? Need to convert CAD->USD on 2024-03-01.\n\nCAD->USD on 2024-03-01:\n- Direct CAD->USD: none\n- Reverse USD->CAD: none\n\nTry pivots (GBP, EUR):\n1. GBP pivot:\n   - CAD->GBP on 2024-03-01: Direct none, Reverse GBP->CAD on 2024-03-01 = 1.7200, so rate = 1/1.7200 = 0.5813953488\n   - GBP->USD on 2024-03-01: Direct none, Reverse USD->GBP on 2024-03-01 = 0.8000, so rate = 1/0.8000 = 1.25\n   - CAD->USD via GBP = 0.5813953488 * 1.25 = 0.7267441860 (rounded to 10dp)\n\nSo FX exists via GBP pivot. T015 is valid.\n\nA1002 valid transactions:\n- T004 (row 4): +50 USD, PLAN_B ALL\n- T011 (row 12): +5 USD, PLAN_B ALL\n- T015 (row 16): +100 CAD -> USD, PLAN_B ALL\n\nT004: fee = 0.10 + 0.002 * 50 = 0.10 + 0.10 = 0.20. Round to 2dp: 0.20. Clamp [0.10, 2.00]: 0.20\nadjusted = 50 - 0.20 = 49.80\n\nT011: fee = 0.10 + 0.002 * 5 = 0.10 + 0.01 = 0.11. Round: 0.11. Clamp: 0.11\nadjusted = 5 - 0.11 = 4.89\n\nT015: \n- CAD->USD via GBP:\n  - CAD->GBP: 1/1.72 = 0.5813953488 (let me verify: 1/1.72 = 0.5813953488372...)\n  - GBP->USD: 1/0.80 = 1.25\n\n  Rate = 0.5813953488 * 1.25 = 0.726744186 (let me verify)\n  0.5813953488 * 1.25 = 0.726744186\n\n100 * 0.726744186 = 72.6744186\nfee = 0.10 + 0.002 * 72.6744186 = 0.10 + 0.1453488372 = 0.2453488372\nRound to 2dp: 0.25\nClamp [0.10, 2.00]: 0.25\nadjusted = 72.6744186 - 0.25 = 72.4244186\nRound to 2dp: 72.42\n\nWait, I need to check my code again. Let me re-read it:\n\nIn my code:\n```j