-10.00 + 9.20 = -0.80\nRounded to 2dp: -0.80\n\nMy output shows A1003 = -0.80. \n\nNow A1004 (USD, PLAN_C applies to CREDIT):\n\nValid transactions for A1004:\n- T009 (row 10): REVERSED (T010 reverses it)\n- T010 (row 11): REVERSED (it reverses T009)\n\nBoth are reversed, so no valid transactions.\n\nA1004:\nstart_balance = 36500.00\nNo valid transactions.\neod_balance = 36500.00\n\nAPR: base_apr = 0.01005, tier_threshold = 999999.00\neod_balance (36500.00) < tier_threshold (999999.00), so no tier_apr.\nNo promo (promo_days = 0).\napr = 0.01005\n\ndaily_interest_raw = 36500 * 0.01005 / 365 = 366.825 / 365 = 1.0049315068... (10dp)\n= 1.0049315068\n\ndaily_interest (rounded to 2dp) = 1.00\n\nMy output shows A1004 = 1.00 for daily_interest, apr = 0.010050. \n\nNow let me verify the exceptions more carefully. Looking at my output:\n\n```\nrow_num,tx_id,reason\n2,T002,AFTER_BIZ_DATE\n3,T003,PENDING\n5,T004,DUPLICATE\n6,T005,REVERSED\n7,T006,REVERSED\n9,T008,REVERSAL_MISSING\n10,T009,REVERSED\n11,T010,REVERSED\n13,T012,AFTER_BIZ_DATE\n18,T016,DUPLICATE\n19,T017,REVERSED\n20,T018,REVERSED\n```\n\nWait, I'm missing row 14 (T015) - but that's valid, so shouldn't be in exceptions.\nWhat about row 17 (T016 for A9999)? Account doesn't exist, but should it be in exceptions?\n\nThe spec lists these exception reasons: REVERSED, REVERSAL_MISSING, FX_MISSING, AFTER_BIZ_DATE, status!=POSTED, DUPLICATE. There's no reason for \"account not found\". So I think it's correct to silently skip row 17.\n\nBut wait - let me re-check the requirements. The problem says \"Use these reasons in file order\". Let me see if there's any indication that we should skip invalid accounts...\n\nLooking at the data, row 17 has T016 for A9999. A9999 doesn't exist in accounts.csv. The reasons listed don't include anything for missing accounts. So I assume we silently skip it (don't add to exceptions), but we still count it as skipped.\n\nHmm, but then what about row 18 (T016 for A1001)? It should be DUPLICATE because T016 appeared before (row 17). My code does mark row 18 as DUPLICATE.\n\nThe issue is: when I mark row 18 as DUPLICATE, do I count row 17 as skipped or not?\n\nLooking at my output: skipped_txs = 13. Let me count:\n- Row 2: skipped (AFTER_BIZ_DATE)\n- Row 3: skipped (PENDING)\n- Row 5: skipped (DUPLICATE)\n- Row 6: skipped (REVERSED)\n- Row 7: skipped (REVERSED)\n- Row 9: skipped (REVERSAL_MISSING)\n- Row 10: skipped (REVERSED)\n- Row 11: skipped (REVERSED)\n- Row 13: skipped (AFTER_BIZ_DATE)\n- Row 17: skipped (no reason, but account doesn't exist)\n- Row 18: skipped (DUPLICATE)\n- Row 19: skipped (REVERSED)\n- Row 20: skipped (REVERSED)\n\nThat's 13 skipped transactions. And I have 20 data rows, so 20 - 13 = 7 valid. But wait:\n\nValid transactions:\n- Row 1 (T001): valid\n- Row 4 (T004): valid\n- Row 8 (T007): valid\n- Row 12 (T011): valid\n- Row 14 (T013): valid\n- Row 15 (T014): valid\n- Row 16 (T015): valid\n\nThat's 7 valid transactions. 20 - 7 = 13 skipped. \n\nNow let me run the job again to verify idempotency:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4226,"cache_read_input_tokens":32772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4226,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"304a76bf-dcaf-4449-b09e-066619c7b878","uuid":"38a45b05-a9a1-4223-b77d-ae8d36fa696c"}
